## 3. Hono on Workers + routing to a DO + coexisting with the assets binding

**Source:** https://hono.dev/docs/getting-started/cloudflare-workers (last updated 2026-07-23)

### Hono app + WebSocket upgrade to a DO

```ts
import { Hono } from "hono";

// `wrangler types --env-interface CloudflareBindings` generates worker-configuration.d.ts
// with this interface from your wrangler.jsonc bindings.
const app = new Hono<{ Bindings: CloudflareBindings }>();

// Static SPA + API + WebSocket on one Worker.
// Assets-first routing (run_worker_first false, default): Hono only runs for
// /api/*, /ws/*, and any path that doesn't match a static asset.

app.get("/api/health", (c) => c.json({ ok: true }));

app.get("/ws/:roomId", async (c) => {
  const upgrade = c.req.header("Upgrade");
  if (upgrade?.toLowerCase() !== "websocket") {
    return c.body(null, 426);
  }
  const roomId = c.req.param("roomId");
  // idFromName gives a stable DO id per room name.
  const id = c.env.GAME_ROOM.idFromName(roomId);
  const stub = c.env.GAME_ROOM.get(id);
  // Forward the upgrade request; the DO returns status 101 + the client WS.
  return stub.fetch(c.req.raw);
});

export default app; // Hono's fetch handler is the Worker's fetch handler.
```

### Getting the DO stub
- `env.GAME_ROOM.idFromName(roomId)` → `DurableObjectId`
- `env.GAME_ROOM.get(id)` → `DurableObjectStub`
- Then `stub.fetch(request)` (HTTP) or call RPC methods directly on `stub` (e.g. `await stub.someMethod(args)`) — RPC is available since compat date `
